# Security and privacy

## Local-first

Default: no outbound send of repository code, paths, or metadata. Optional LLM: `ALLOW_LLM` + keys in `.env.example`; tool outputs pass through `ci_security.sanitize_for_llm`.

## Tokens

`CI_GITHUB_TOKEN` for private clones via `GIT_CONFIG_*` env (see `ci_parsers` git clone). Never log tokens; detect-secrets baseline at `.secrets.baseline`.

## Read-only sources

Indexing and `ci projects remove` never delete user source directories (only managed clones). Server mode: `CI_PROJECT_ROOTS` + `CI_API_KEY`.

## Content safety

Untrusted repo text: no HTML rendering of source. See [docs/SECURITY.md](docs/SECURITY.md) and [docs/private-repos.md](docs/private-repos.md).
